{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 1, :comments ["<b>Word of YHWH that came to Hosea son of Beeri</b> — This Hosea is among the distinguished prophets of HaShem. For Yitzhaki spoke improperly in his book concerning him, saying: he is the son of Beeri, for Beeri is [the same as] Beerah, since it is found written: <b>and Beerah his son</b>, and Be'eri is not Be'erah, for the addition of a letter changes the name, like Ziph and Ziphah. Furthermore, there is no rule in the holy tongue to call a person by a city's name as a proper name, unless it is in a general sense like Bat Zion; rather, the demonym would relate to the city, like Shomroni. Two things pressured him to say thus: the first, that he found in Chronicles Beerah son of his [ancestor] whom Tiglath-pileser king of Assyria exiled, who was prince of the Reubenites, and he was the father of this prophet. And the second, that he said <b>and to visit upon Jacob his ways</b> — for he explains this of Jacob our father, that he removed the birthright from Reuben. But his explanation is not as he supposed, and behold, he forgot what is written of Hosea son of Beeri: <b>and he did the evil in the eyes of HaShem</b>, and Yitzhaki said: that he took a wife of harlotry."], :book :hosea, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 1, :notes {0 "The cited phrase 'ובאר אלים יללתה' appears corrupt in the source; translated hyper-literally. 'היצחקי' resolved by inference to Yitzhaki, likely referring to Ibn Janah or a similar medieval commentator."}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Hosea -- Daat" "http://www.daat.ac.il/daat/olam_hatanah/mefaresh.asp?book=15&perek=1&mefaresh=ezra"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T18:49:47.758469199Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}